  "rule": "complex.cif = retained protein chains + peptide + metals and monatomic ions only. Kept: any component in peptide.cif (the peptide's own covalent structure - caps, staples, thioethers, linkers, glycopeptide glycans), any component sharing a label_asym_id with such a component (a branched entity is one molecule per SPEC sec.7, so an O-glycan's GAL/SIA go with the A2G that is bonded to the peptide), anything reachable from the peptide by a transitive chain of covalent bonds - _struct_conn covale/disulf or an unannotated bond at BOND_INFER_SCALE 1.25 x sum of covalent radii - which is what keeps a lipid tail bonded to a moiety that is itself bonded to the peptide, a MONATOMIC ion (exactly one heavy atom, element a metal per corpus_chem.METALS or a halide F/CL/BR/I; UNX/UNL denied), and a terminal cap covalently bonded to a retained receptor chain. Removed: every other non-polymer - crystallisation additives including the polyatomic anions SO4, PO4, NO3, SCN, ACT, glycans, lipids, UNX placeholders and curated biological cofactors. Curated cofactors are additionally written to complex_cofactors.cif so the decision stays reversible per entry.",
